HARD CONSTRAINTS (dec 027 item 1 fidelity; do not touch): no PIP_* env prefixes, the Docker-order setup path (editable install before base injection), the pinned starter docker_image, enable_internet=False, the setup-only mode and its tests. All new hooks are pure observation wrappers: they call the original with identical args, return its value unchanged and re-raise its exceptions unchanged. No harness behavior change except the explicit verification skip below.

1. SKIP_VERIFICATION template constant (default True), substituted by timing_push.sh (add flag --with-verification to set False; keep --dry-run working). When True, the kernel replaces swegemma.evaluate.verify_task with a stub that starts no container and runs no tests, returning the same type/shape the real verify_task returns (read the installed source: /home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/swegemma/evaluate.py and harness/verification.py) with resolved False and test exit code None. A row must NOT get error='Harness task failure' merely because verification was skipped: set verification_skipped=true on the row and only flag real harness/agent-runner errors (e.g. agent_runner exceptions, ContainerSetupError, cleanup exceptions). should_stop must use verification timeout 0 when skipped.

2. Per-task Phase-1 timing (all perf_counter, stored per task in the ContextVar state):
 a. Wrap swegemma.harness.agent_runner module globals sandbox_start, sandbox_stop, sandbox_exec (they are imported names at agent_runner.py:47-49 and called at :493, :1057-1061, :1118). Record sandbox_start begin and sandbox_stop end timestamps and durations.
 b. Agent clock: agent_runner does `import asyncio` and builds `asyncio.timeout(timeout_sec)` at :725, entered later. Replace agent_runner's module attribute `asyncio` with a proxy object that forwards every attribute to the real asyncio except `timeout`, which returns an async context manager wrapping the real asyncio.timeout(delay) and records: delay, enter time, exit time, and fired = (real cm.expired() if available) or the exit exception is TimeoutError. Must not swallow or alter exceptions. Restore the original attribute in the existing finally block.
 c. Row fields (add, keep all existing fields): agent_timeout_seconds (delay), agent_clock_seconds (exit-enter), agent_timeout_fired (bool), finalization_seconds = sandbox_stop end - timeout-context exit (covers fallback git add -N / git diff / strip / stop), finalization_exec = list of {cmd: first 40 chars, duration_s, rc or exception type name} for sandbox_exec calls after the timeout exit, teardown_seconds = sandbox_stop duration, phase1_wall_seconds = sandbox_stop end - sandbox_start begin (if a wrapper did not fire, fall back to the _run_agent_sandbox duration and set phase1_source='run_agent_sandbox' else 'sandbox_wrappers'), pre_agent_seconds = timeout enter - sandbox_start begin, post_phase1_seconds = total - phase1_wall_seconds, patch_submitted (context.patch_submitted), fallback_patch_used (not submitted and non-empty patch). Null-safe when hooks did not fire (e.g. setup failure).
 d. The header's vllm_startup_seconds must be populated (it is currently declared None; set it after start_server) and documented in fields. Document every new row field in header fields.

